    "details": {
        "name": "MOB.977_DIAG_Condition_Form_Schema_Race",
        "type": "browser",
        "status": "paused",
        "message": "`MOB.977` **The only test that reproduces bugs \u00a742** \u2014 a condition form's first Submit after a page load does nothing.\n- \ud83d\uded1 **It asserts a BUG: red means the bug is gone.** If `\u2b50 \u00a742 REPRODUCED` fails, read `Conditions/Form.tsx` and `components/utils/hooks/index.ts` \u2014 if the schema is passed with `withDynamicSchema` now, \u00a742 is fixed: delete this test and the bug, and drop the `soft` sentinels in MOB.385/386/390/391.\n- \u2b50 **The test is the absence of a step.** It deep-links `/work/<id>` and never visits `/work`, whose prefetch loads `WorkStageCondition`. Adding a warm-up here deletes the only thing it tests.\n- The proof is a `/graphql` read \u2014 an armed Submit, an open modal, and a server that still holds the resting score. Then the SAME form, reopened with the schema cached, saves: that contrast is what makes it \u00a742 rather than a broken form.\n- \u26a0\ufe0f **It is a race** (bugs \u00a742: the add path failed 2 of 3 and 3 of 3 on Datadog). One red run means read the source, not that the bug is fixed.\n- \ud83d\uded1 Not in any scheduled suite, deliberately. Self-restoring (`always`); `preflight.py mob39x` guards the resting score.",
